Package differences: the one shape where the port and the original disagree, an excluded Go file that does not
parse, after which the original checks no excluded file, Go or other, and the port checks every one. A finding only
the port makes is recorded on its line after the original's testing hack, a spaced `// ERROR` comment, which ends
what either side reads of the line. It is an archive because one file does not parse, and cohere's gofmt guard reads
every Go file under testdata.
-- src/differences/differences.go --
// Package differences holds the excluded files around one that does not parse.
package differences
-- src/differences/before.go --
// An excluded file named before the broken one, which both sides check.

//go:build never

package differences

// +build late
-- src/differences/broken.go --
//go:build never

package differences

func {
-- src/differences/checked_after.go --
// An excluded file named after the broken one, which only the port checks.

//go:build never

package differences

// +build late // ERROR // port finds: misplaced +build comment
-- src/differences/excluded.s --
//go:build never
// +build late // ERROR // port finds: misplaced +build comment
#include "textflag.h"
